        <p class="muted">
          The residential figure represents 1,000 homes multiplied by an
          approximately $240,000 Jefferson County median home-value benchmark.
          The selected data-center figures represent announced investments and
          should not be interpreted as assessed property values or annual tax collections.
        </p>

        <p>
          The selected projects have a median announced investment of approximately
          $1.5 billion and a simple average of approximately $3.75 billion. The median
          is approximately 6.25 times the illustrative residential property value,
          while the average is approximately 15.6 times that value.
        </p>

        <p>
          These comparisons demonstrate differences in capital scale. They do not,
          by themselves, establish which form of development produces more annual
          tax revenue or greater overall public value.
        </p>


        <h3>Illustrative Residential Tax Benchmark</h3>

        <div class="table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Residential tax benchmark table" tabindex="0">
          <table>
